<title>SOUTH AFRICA: RUGBY UNION-SOUTH AFRICA BEAT BRITISH LIONS 35-16.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-SOUTH AFRICA BEAT BRITISH LIONS 35-16.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa beat the</p>
<p>British Lions 35-16 (haltime 13-9) in the third and final test</p>
<p>at Ellis Park on Saturday. The Lions won the series 2-1.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>South Africa - Tries: Percival Montgomery, Joost van der</p>
<p>Westhuizen, Andre Snyman, Pieter Rossouw. Conversions: Jannie de</p>
<p>Beer (2), Henry Honiball. Penalties: De Beer (3).</p>
<p>British Lions - Try: Matt Dawson. Conversion: Neil Jenkins.</p>
<p>Penalties: Jenkins (3).</p>
</text>
